Constellation submits this motion for leave and answer1 to emphasize one point: if the 
Commission’s goal is to interconnect loads faster than the current 7-to-10-year timeframe,2 it must 

1 Constellation Energy Generation, LLC (“Constellation”) submits there is good cause to accept this answer to the 
rehearing requests filed by Indicated PJM Transmission Owners and jointly by Exelon Corporation (“Exelon”) and 
FirstEnergy Service Company (“FirstEnergy”) (collectively, Transmission Owner Rehearing Requests) as our 
answer is intended to assist the Commission in its decision making. See, e.g., Tex. E. Transmission, LP, 127 FERC 
¶ 61,162, at P 6 (2009) (finding good cause to accept an answer to a rehearing request because the answer “provides 
information that will assist [the Commission] in [its] decision-making process”). 
2 See, e.g., Comments of Talen Energy Corp., Docket No. AD24-11-000, Analysis Group Report at 12 n.43 (Oct. 28, 
2024) (describing wait times to plan, design, site and construct a new grid connection to be as long as seven years 
for Dominion and seven to ten years for AEP).
